topics.detail:
AI Misuse argues that AI is overused in search engines. AI-generated artwork is used to bully artists. AI Overuse argues that AI can't automate basic tasks. AI should be used as a tool not a replacement.

@pulsarbird.bsky.social: “Speaking of AI, I'm also continually amazed at how AI can't actually automate basic tasks in my (professional) job. e.g: syncing clips into a multicam using audio. I've never gotten premiere to do this successfully. Sounds like the perfect use for AI yeah?”

AI Misuse (60.6%) says AI is being used improperly. AI Overuse (39.4%) says AI is being overused.

AI Not Productive argues that AI replaces human productivity with inferior results. AI cannot produce original content. Artists Reject AI argues that AI art lacks human touch.

@walmsley.bsky.social: “by freeing humans from the need to create art so that they can more efficiently engage in productive labor, generative AI is the first ontologically Calvinist technology”

AI Not Productive (65.6%) says AI is not productive. Artists Reject AI (34.4%) says AI art lacks human touch.

AI Harms World argues that AI can displace work in time and make it more frustrating. Relying on AI can lead to lower quality work and overlook important aspects like relationship and authenticity. AI Impact argues that AI brings new opportunities but tough times for young people without wealth. AI discussion is needlessly pessimistic. Some people prefer AI over raising kids. AI has a unique life cycle. AI robots may steal human money.

@ealgumby.bsky.social: “The point of the episode is PARTICULARLY PERTINENT TODAY, as we struggle with the role of AI... Here's the thing: AI can be 'right' (commit no mistakes), and STILL LOSE! If one is adept (as I might be) at predicting AI response, it becomes a joke to make it 'lose' all the time.”

AI Harms World (78.1%) says AI is harmful to the world. AI Impact (21.9%) says AI affects human life.

World.detail:
Russia Aggression argues that Russia uses NATO as an excuse to expand. Russia started the war in Ukraine. Russia's presence at G20 is unacceptable. Easing economic pressure on Russia prolongs the war. Russia is spreading disinformation against candidates who support Ukraine. Russia is imposing its will on the West. Russian Aggression argues that Russia represents itself poorly on the world stage. Russia uses child soldiers. Russia commits war crimes.

@paulusthewoodgnome.bsky.social: “"Let me say this directly to the Russian foreign minister. We know you are the aggressor. We know you started this war four and a half years ago with the full-scale invasion of Ukraine. Putin thought then he would win this war easily.”

Russia Aggression (52.8%) says Russia is the aggressor. Russian Aggression (47.2%) says Russia is committing atrocities.

Israel Condemned argues that Israel's government is accused of genocide. Israel is blamed for killing civilians in Gaza. Netanyahu Opposition argues that Opposition can beat Netanyahu if they work with Arab peers. The problem in Israel is not just Netanyahu. There are Israelis who oppose Netanyahu's actions in Gaza.

@luxalptraum.com: “Fundamentally if Jewish Israelis want to continue to argue that they are not living in an apartheid state, forming a coalition government with Arab parties is a great way to prove the haters wrong”

Israel Condemned (62.8%) says Israel is criticized for its actions. Netanyahu Opposition (37.2%) says Netanyahu can be beaten if opponents work together.

Technology.detail:
AI Coding argues that AI should not be used in coding. AI Security Risks argues that AI poses security risks.

@bookofoak.bsky.social: “I honestly do not care if AI is used during the coding process, just that it appears nowhere as an *user feature*. Or at least fucking make it opt in.”

AI Coding (83.9%) says AI should not be used in coding. AI Security Risks (16.1%) says AI poses security risks.

AI Not Welcome argues that AI undermines human productivity. AI is a productivity trap. AI compromises privacy and security. AI Lacks Soul argues that AI art prioritizes clout and money over creative process. AI usage undermines human mental capability and agency.

@carnage4life.bsky.social: “In the 1980s, PCs were everywhere but productivity gains were nowhere to be found until the 1990s. The internet similarly took years to deliver an economic payoff. This is the Productivity J-Curve.”

AI Not Welcome (66.7%) says AI is not beneficial. AI Lacks Soul (33.3%) says AI art lacks human joy and love.

AI Backlash argues that AI will slow down when it affects companies' profits. AI will crash markets and become unprofitable. AI will face regulatory issues with building code compliance. AI Impact argues that AI affects learning and work.

@alerigolon.bsky.social: “These tech goons will only slow down with the AI nonsense when it starts hitting their bottom line in hard ways. Looks like it’s now for Google”

AI Backlash (60%) says AI will face financial setbacks. AI Impact (40%) says AI affects learning and work.
